md`# brain-feedback

Feedback about the Brain's page, written on the page. A note placed with \`@tomlarkworthy/annotate\` is filed as a \`feedback\` issue of \`brain-issues\`, and from then on the note shows that issue.

| | |
|---|---|
| Where | The Brain's own address, with the owner signed in. Not a portal, not a page opened with \`#verify=\`, not a file. \`feedbackOn\` says which. |
| Start one | The page menu, Annotate, Feedback; or select text and press the chip \`feedback\`. Click what the note is about, write, press **File**. |
| The default | A note that annotate makes with no kind is made a feedback note here (\`feedbackDefault\`): Note in the menu, the chip \`annotate\`, Annotate in the palette. The owner, 2026-10-11: "yes make it the default". A plain note has no File and nothing sends it; three of his were written as plain notes and taken as filed. A note of another kind (\`switchboard\`) is as before. So this page has no plain note. |
| What is filed | \`issue.open\` with kind \`feedback\`, the label \`annotation\`, the id \`fb-<note id>\`, the first line as the title, and \`about\` the Worker whose module was clicked (\`brain\` when it is none). The body is the text, one sentence that says where, and the anchor as JSON in a fence named \`annotation\`. |
| On page load | \`issue.list?label=annotation\`, then \`issue.get\` for each, and a note is placed for each at its anchor. Asked again every 30 s while the tab is visible; an issue is read again only when its \`updated_at\` moved. |
| What a note shows | Two things: the request as it was written, whole, and the latest state of the work with the id of the issue that state is of. Nothing of the comments, links or reviews (Tom, 2026-10-11: "the original request needs to be show. I think the jsut the latest state is good"). When the issue is done, the reason it was closed with as well. |
| Gathered | The loop closes a feedback issue when it has made it part of a project or linked it to another issue, which is before the work is done. Such a note reads the state of the first of those issues that is still open, with its id (\`building\` \`dashboards-…\`), follows those issues (\`feedbackFollows\`: its parent, and each issue it says a link of), and has no Remove. They are not in the list, so each is read with \`issue.get\` on every ask. One step: an issue they are part of in turn is not followed. |
| Closed | An issue closed with a reason and no parent or link reads its state and the reason for ${feedbackLimits.waitMs / 60000} minutes from the close, with the time Remove comes and no Remove: the loop closes an issue and links it afterwards, 15.5 s apart on the first note filed. The time is the page's clock against the event's. |
| Done | The note reads **Done**, and has **Remove**, when the issue is closed and so is every issue it follows; one that follows none, when those minutes have passed. The reason shown is the one each of those was closed with, after its id and state (\`proj done: …\`, \`proj rejected: …\`); the issue's own when it follows none. |
| Remove | On a done issue, Remove (or the note's own ×) takes the label \`annotation\` off with \`issue.label\`, so no page loads the note again. The issue stays in the record. On an open, gathered or just closed issue the × hides the note until the page is loaded again. A note not yet filed is deleted. |

No Worker and no table: the record is the issue. The label is the switch, so anyone who may label can take a note off every page; the loop's briefs say not to.

The cells of a note are kept in this module (\`home\` of the kind), not in the module the note points at. A note on a Worker's panel is then not part of that Worker's source when the page exports it.

A note's box can be moved; the new place is not kept.

**A note not yet filed** is kept in this browser, since 2026-10-11: its text, its anchor and its box, in \`localStorage\` under \`brain_feedback_drafts ADDRESS\` (\`feedbackKept\`), written on each keystroke. A note is a cell of the page and the page keeps none, so a reload takes the note itself; on the first ask after a load each kept one is placed again where it was, as a new note with the text in its box, and it is filed under the id of the note it was first typed in. When the cell \`feedback\` runs again on a page, the note is still there and its box has the text. The copy goes when the note is filed, emptied or removed. It is this browser's alone: another browser, or one that refuses \`localStorage\`, has no copy, and a box moved after the last keystroke comes back where it was at that keystroke.
`
// %%
// The Brain's own page, the owner signed in. A verify page runs a Worker's tests and is left alone.
feedbackOn = !!brainOrigin && !brainPortal && !!(brainWho && brainWho.owner) && !/[#&]verify=/.test(location.hash)
// %%
feedbackLimits = ({ title: 120, text: 4000, shown: 400, everyMs: 30000, waitMs: 300000, label: "annotation", kind: "feedback", home: "@tomlarkworthy/brain-feedback", fence: "`".repeat(3) + "annotation\n", says: "Annotated on the Brain's page: " })
// %%
// One sentence a reader of the issue can act on without the page.
// near: the text of the element under the note's tip, for a note that marks no text of its own.
feedbackWhere = (anchor = {}, near = "") =>
  feedbackLimits.says +
  [anchor.module && `module \`${anchor.module}\``, anchor.cell && `cell \`${anchor.cell}\``, anchor.quote && anchor.quote.exact ? `at the text "${String(anchor.quote.exact).slice(0, 200)}"` : near && `on the element that reads "${String(near).replace(/\s+/g, " ").trim().slice(0, 120)}"`].filter(Boolean).concat(anchor.module || anchor.cell ? [] : ["no cell"]).join(", ") + "."
// %%
feedbackBody = (text, where, near = "") => `${String(text).trim()}\n\n${feedbackWhere(where.anchor, near)}\n\n${feedbackLimits.fence}${JSON.stringify(where)}\n${"`".repeat(3)}`
// %%
// { text, anchor, box } of a body feedbackBody wrote, or null.
feedbackParse = (body) => {
  const s = String(body || ""), at = s.lastIndexOf(feedbackLimits.fence);
  if (at < 0) return null;
  const from = at + feedbackLimits.fence.length, end = s.indexOf("\n" + "`".repeat(3), from);
  try {
    const where = JSON.parse(s.slice(from, end < 0 ? undefined : end));
    if (!where || typeof where.anchor !== "object" || !where.anchor) return null;
    const head = s.slice(0, at), said = head.lastIndexOf("\n\n" + feedbackLimits.says);
    return { text: (said < 0 ? head : head.slice(0, said)).trim(), anchor: where.anchor, box: where.box || null };
  } catch {
    return null;
  }
}
// %%
// The issues a closed issue is waited for in: what it is part of, and what it says a link of. One step, not theirs in turn.
feedbackFollows = (issue) => (issue && issue.closed ? [...new Set([issue.parent, ...(issue.links || []).map((l) => l.to)].filter(Boolean))] : [])
// %%
// What a note shows of an issue's events: the last one that says something, and the reason it was closed with.
// followed: what issue.get answered for each of feedbackFollows(issue), in that order; undefined for one not read.
// done: closed, and so is each issue it is followed in. gathered: closed, and one of those is not, or was not read.
// A closed issue that follows none is done once it has been closed for waitMs, and settling until then: the loop
// closes an issue and then links it (15.5 s apart on fb-a2kw99i9wy), and Remove in between would be for good.
feedbackProgress = (ticket, followed = [], { now = Date.now(), waitMs = feedbackLimits.waitMs } = {}) => {
  const { issue, events = [] } = ticket;
  const who = (by = {}) => (String(by.holder || "").startsWith("secret:") ? by.holder.slice(7).replace(/^issues-/, "") : by.caller || "");
  const said = (e) => e.body || e.reason || (e.type === "linked" ? `${e.remove ? "no longer " : ""}${e.rel}${e.to ? " " + e.to : ""}` : e.type === "swapped" ? "moved to another workflow" : "");
  // Not the loop's cost record, a comment `cost {…}` after each round, which says nothing to the owner.
  const lastOf = (t) => [...(t.events || [])].reverse().find((e) => e.type !== "opened" && said(e) && !/^cost \{/.test(e.body || ""));
  const closingOf = (t) => [...(t.events || [])].reverse().find((e) => e.type === "moved" && e.to === t.issue.state);
  const reasonOf = (t) => ((e) => (e ? e.reason || "" : ""))(closingOf(t));
  const follows = feedbackFollows(issue), read = (id) => followed[follows.indexOf(id)];
  const stateOf = (id) => ((t) => (t ? `: ${t.issue.state}` : ""))(read(id));
  const until = ((e) => (e ? e.at : issue.updated_at || 0))(closingOf(ticket)) + waitMs;
  const done = !!issue.closed && (follows.length ? follows.every((id) => read(id) && read(id).issue.closed) : now >= until);
  const gathered = !!issue.closed && !done && follows.length > 0, settling = !!issue.closed && !done && !follows.length;
  const links = [issue.parent && `part of ${issue.parent}${stateOf(issue.parent)}`, ...(issue.links || []).map((l) => `${l.rel} ${l.to}${stateOf(l.to)}`)].filter(Boolean);
  // The later of the issue's own last event and those of the issues it is followed in, which is named.
  const last = [[null, lastOf(ticket)], ...follows.map((id) => [id, read(id) && lastOf(read(id))])].filter(([, e]) => e).sort((x, y) => y[1].at - x[1].at)[0];
  const reason = !issue.closed || gathered ? "" : follows.length ? follows.map((id) => `${id} ${read(id).issue.state}${reasonOf(read(id)) ? ": " + reasonOf(read(id)) : ""}`).join("\n") : reasonOf(ticket);
  // Where the work is now: the first issue it is followed in that is still open, else the issue itself.
  const open = follows.find((id) => read(id) && !read(id).issue.closed);
  const where = done ? { state: "Done", id: issue.id } : gathered ? (open ? { state: read(open).issue.state, id: open } : { state: "gathered", id: follows[0] }) : { state: issue.state, id: issue.id };
  return { state: issue.state, closed: !!issue.closed, done, gathered, settling, until, links, reason, where, last: last ? { who: who(last[1].by), at: last[1].at, type: last[1].type, text: (last[0] ? last[0] + ": " : "") + said(last[1]) } : null };
}
// %%
// The notes of one page. client: issue.* calls. store: annotate's (create, remove, patch, get, all, refresh).
// kept: the browser's copy of the notes not yet filed (feedbackKept); with none, a draft is lost on a reload.
feedbackApp = ({ client, store, kept = { get: () => null, set: () => {} }, about = () => "brain", near = () => "", limits = feedbackLimits, now = () => Date.now() }) => {
  // tickets: issue id to what issue.get answered. of: note id to issue id. hidden: open issues whose note was closed here.
  const tickets = new Map(), of = new Map(), els = new Map(), drafts = new Map(), says = new Map(), hidden = new Set(), filing = new Set();
  let busy = false, placedAgain = false;
  // The copy: a name to { text, anchor, box }. The name is the id of the note the text was first typed in; a note
  // placed again after a reload has a new id and carries the name as `draft`. names: note id to that name, held past the note.
  const names = new Map();
  const nameOf = (id) => names.get(id) || ((rec) => (rec ? (names.set(id, rec.draft || id), names.get(id)) : id))(store.get(id));
  const issueOf = (name) => "fb-" + name.toLowerCase().replace(/[^a-z0-9-]/g, "").slice(0, 36);
  const keptAll = () => {
    try {
      const all = kept.get();
      return all && typeof all === "object" && !Array.isArray(all) ? all : {};
    } catch (e) {
      return {};
    }
  };
  const keep = (name, entry) => {
    try {
      const all = keptAll();
      if (!entry && !(name in all)) return;
      entry ? (all[name] = entry) : delete all[name];
      kept.set(all);
    } catch (e) {}
  };
  const usable = (e) => !!e && typeof e === "object" && typeof e.text === "string" && !!e.text.trim() && !!e.anchor && typeof e.anchor === "object";
  // A note that is still a cell (the app was made again on the page) has its text from the copy.
  const first = keptAll();
  for (const a of store.all()) {
    if (a.kind !== limits.kind) continue;
    if (a.issue) of.set(a.id, a.issue);
    else if (usable(first[nameOf(a.id)])) drafts.set(a.id, first[nameOf(a.id)].text);
  }
  // Once for an app, on its first ask, when annotate knows the kind: a kept text with no note here was typed before
  // the page was loaded again, and its note is placed where it was.
  const placeAgain = () => {
    const all = keptAll(), here = new Set(store.all().flatMap((a) => [a.id, a.draft]));
    for (const [name, e] of Object.entries(all)) {
      if (here.has(name) || !usable(e)) continue;
      const a = store.create(e.anchor, { kind: limits.kind, draft: name, ...(e.box && typeof e.box === "object" ? { box: e.box } : {}) });
      if (a) (names.set(a.id, name), drafts.set(a.id, e.text.slice(0, limits.text)));
    }
  };
  const get = async (iss) => {
    const r = await client.query("issue.get", { id: iss });
    tickets.set(iss, r);
    return r;
  };
  const cut = (s, n) => (String(s).length > n ? String(s).slice(0, n) + "…" : String(s));
  const has = async (id) => (await store.refresh(), !!store.get(id));
  const progress = (t) => feedbackProgress(t, feedbackFollows(t.issue).map((f) => tickets.get(f)), { now: now(), waitMs: limits.waitMs });
  const view = (id) => {
    const iss = of.get(id), t = iss && tickets.get(iss), muted = "color:var(--theme-foreground-muted)";
    if (!iss) {
      const box = htl.html`<textarea rows="4" maxlength=${limits.text} placeholder="What is wrong or wanted here" style="font:inherit;width:100%;box-sizing:border-box">${drafts.get(id) || ""}</textarea>`;
      box.oninput = () => {
        drafts.set(id, box.value);
        const rec = store.get(id);
        keep(nameOf(id), rec && box.value.trim() ? { text: box.value, anchor: rec.anchor, box: rec.box } : null);
      };
      return htl.html`<div data-feedback="draft">${box}<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => file(id)}>File</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || "Filed as a feedback issue."}</span></div></div>`;
    }
    if (!t) return htl.html`<div data-feedback="filing" style=${muted}>${iss}…</div>`;
    const p = progress(t), w = feedbackParse(t.issue.body);
    return htl.html`<div data-feedback=${p.done ? "done" : p.gathered ? "gathered" : p.settling ? "closed" : "open"} style=${"border-left:3px solid " + (p.done ? "#2a9d4b" : "var(--theme-foreground-faint)") + ";padding-left:8px"}>
      <div><b>${p.where.state}</b> <code>${p.where.id}</code></div>
      <div data-feedback-asked style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(w ? w.text : t.issue.title, limits.text)}</div>
      ${(p.done || p.settling) && p.reason ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-reason style="white-space:pre-wrap">${cut(p.reason, limits.shown)}</div>` : ""}
      ${p.settling ? htl.html`<div data-feedback-wait style=${muted}>Remove is here from ${new Date(p.until).toLocaleTimeString()}, unless it has been made part of other work by then.</div>` : ""}
      ${p.done ? htl.html`<div style="display:flex;gap:8px;align-items:center;margin-top:4px"><button onclick=${() => remove(id)}>Remove</button><span style=${muted}>${says.get(id) || ""}</span></div>` : ""}
    </div>`;
  };
  const draw = (id) => els.get(id) && els.get(id).replaceChildren(view(id));
  const file = async (id) => {
    const text = String(drafts.get(id) || "").trim(), rec = store.get(id);
    if (!text || !rec) return (says.set(id, text ? "The note is gone." : "Write something first."), draw(id));
    // Named for the note the text was first typed in, so a second tab that has the same draft opens the same issue.
    const name = nameOf(id), iss = issueOf(name);
    of.set(id, iss);
    filing.add(iss);
    draw(id);
    try {
      await client.procedure("issue.open", { key: "annotation/" + name, id: iss, title: cut(text.split("\n")[0], limits.title), body: feedbackBody(text, { anchor: rec.anchor, box: rec.box }, near(rec)), kind: "feedback", about: about(rec.anchor), labels: [limits.label] });
      await get(iss);
      drafts.delete(id);
      keep(name, null);
      says.delete(id);
      store.patch(id, { issue: iss });
    } catch (e) {
      of.delete(id);
      says.set(id, "issue.open was refused: " + e.message);
    }
    filing.delete(iss);
    draw(id);
  };
  // Places a note for each labeled issue that has none here, and takes away a note whose issue lost the label.
  const sync = async () => {
    if (busy) return;
    busy = true;
    try {
      if (!placedAgain) {
        placedAgain = true;
        try {
          placeAgain();
        } catch (e) {
          console.warn("brain-feedback: a kept draft was not placed again: " + e.message);
        }
      }
      const listed = (await client.query("issue.list", { label: limits.label, limit: 200 })).issues.filter((i) => !i.hidden);
      for (const i of listed) if (!tickets.has(i.id) || tickets.get(i.id).issue.updated_at !== i.updated_at) await get(i.id);
      // A draft here whose issue is in the list was filed from another tab: the note is that issue's, and no second is placed.
      for (const a of store.all()) {
        const iss = a.kind === limits.kind && !a.issue && !of.has(a.id) && issueOf(nameOf(a.id));
        if (!iss || !listed.some((i) => i.id === iss)) continue;
        of.set(a.id, iss);
        drafts.delete(a.id);
        keep(nameOf(a.id), null);
        store.patch(a.id, { issue: iss });
      }
      // What a closed one is followed in is not listed here, so nothing says it moved: each is read on every ask.
      for (const f of new Set(listed.flatMap((i) => feedbackFollows(tickets.get(i.id).issue)))) await get(f).catch(() => tickets.delete(f));
      const placed = new Set(of.values()), ids = new Set(listed.map((i) => i.id));
      for (const i of listed) {
        const where = !placed.has(i.id) && !hidden.has(i.id) && feedbackParse(tickets.get(i.id).issue.body);
        if (!where) continue;
        const a = store.create(where.anchor, { kind: limits.kind, issue: i.id, ...(where.box ? { box: where.box } : {}) });
        if (a) of.set(a.id, i.id);
      }
      for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
        if (ids.has(iss) || filing.has(iss)) continue;
        const t = await get(iss).catch(() => null);
        if (t && (t.issue.labels || []).includes(limits.label)) continue;
        of.delete(id);
        tickets.delete(iss);
        els.delete(id);
        store.remove(id);
      }
      // A draft shows nothing of the tracker, and drawing it again would take the box out from under the caret.
      for (const id of els.keys()) if (of.has(id)) draw(id);
    } finally {
      busy = false;
    }
  };
  // Run when the page's notes change. A filed note that is no longer a cell was removed by the reader: when its
  // issue is done (feedbackProgress) the label comes off, and no page loads it again.
  const gone = async () => {
    for (const [id, iss] of [...of]) {
      if (await has(id)) continue;
      of.delete(id);
      els.delete(id);
      const t = tickets.get(iss);
      if (!t) continue;
      if (!progress(t).done) hidden.add(iss);
      else {
        tickets.delete(iss);
        await client.procedure("issue.label", { key: `annotation/${iss}/removed`, id: iss, remove: [limits.label] }).catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: issue.label was refused: " + e.message));
      }
    }
    for (const id of [...drafts.keys()]) if (!of.has(id) && !(await has(id))) (keep(nameOf(id), null), names.delete(id), drafts.delete(id), els.delete(id));
  };
  const remove = async (id) => {
    store.remove(id);
    await gone();
  };
  const note = (id) => {
    const el = htl.html`<div data-feedback-note=${id} style="font:13px var(--sans-serif)"></div>`;
    els.set(id, el);
    draw(id);
    return el;
  };
  // Annotate's menu, palette and selection chip each end in store.create, and the plain note is the first of each.
  // From this call until the function it answers is called, a note created with no kind is of this one.
  const byDefault = () => {
    const create = store.create;
    let on = true;
    const mine = (anchor, fields) => create.call(store, anchor, on && !(fields && (fields.kind || fields.src)) ? { ...fields, kind: limits.kind } : fields);
    mine.byDefault = limits.kind;
    store.create = mine;
    return () => ((on = false), void (store.create === mine && (store.create = create)));
  };
  const kind = { id: limits.kind, label: "Feedback", chip: "feedback", icon: "✉", order: 1, home: limits.home, box: { w: 280 }, note: ({ id }) => `feedbackNote(${JSON.stringify(id)})` };
  return { note, file, sync, gone, remove, byDefault, kind, tickets, of, hidden, drafts };
}
// %%
// The text under a note's tip: the first element there that is in a cell and not in annotate's own layer.
feedbackNear = (rec, { resolve = a2Anchors.resolve, doc = document } = {}) => {
  try {
    const at = resolve(rec.anchor), p = at && (at.kind === "rects" ? at.rects[0] && { x: at.rects[0].left + 2, y: at.rects[0].top + 2 } : at);
    const el = p && doc.elementsFromPoint(p.x, p.y).find((e) => e.closest(".observablehq") && !e.closest("[data-a2-layer],[data-a2-root]"));
    return el ? el.textContent || "" : "";
  } catch {
    return "";
  }
}
// %%
// The browser's copy of the notes not yet filed, one item for each Brain's address. A browser may refuse it; a draft
// is then lost on a reload. globalThis.localStorage, not the bare name: a cell that names it has no value without a browser.
feedbackKept = (brain = "") => ((name) => ({
  name,
  get: () => {
    try {
      return JSON.parse(globalThis.localStorage.getItem(name));
    } catch (e) {
      return null;
    }
  },
  set: (all) => {
    try {
      Object.keys(all || {}).length ? globalThis.localStorage.setItem(name, JSON.stringify(all)) : globalThis.localStorage.removeItem(name);
    } catch (e) {}
  }
}))("brain_feedback_drafts " + brain)
// %%
feedback = feedbackOn ? feedbackApp({ client: brainClient, store: a2Store, kept: feedbackKept(brainOrigin), near: feedbackNear, about: (anchor) => ((m) => (m ? m.worker : "brain"))(((brainModules && brainModules.modules) || []).find((m) => m.module === (anchor || {}).module)) }) : null
// %%
// The cell a note is: annotate writes `feedbackNote("<id>")` into this module for the kind below.
feedbackNote = (id) => (feedback ? feedback.note(id) : htl.html`<i>Feedback notes are for the owner, signed in at the Brain's address.</i>`)
// %%
feedbackKind = {
  if (!feedback) return "off: " + (!brainOrigin ? "not a Brain's address" : brainPortal ? "a portal" : !(brainWho && brainWho.owner) ? "the owner is not signed in" : "a verify page");
  plugins.add("annotate-kinds", feedback.kind, { invalidation });
  return "registered the kind feedback";
}
// %%
// The owner, 2026-10-11, asked whether Feedback should be the kind of a note he makes on his page: "yes make it the default".
feedbackDefault = {
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  invalidation.then(feedback.byDefault());
  return "a note made with no kind is of the kind " + feedbackLimits.kind;
}
// %%
feedbackSync = {
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  // A note placed before annotate knows the kind would be written into the module it points at.
  feedbackKind;
  for (let i = 0; i < 400 && !a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind); i++) await new Promise((r) => setTimeout(r, 25));
  if (!a2Store.kindOf(feedbackLimits.kind)) return "annotate has no kind " + feedbackLimits.kind;
  const tick = () => document.visibilityState === "visible" && feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  const timer = setInterval(tick, feedbackLimits.everyMs);
  invalidation.then(() => clearInterval(timer));
  await feedback.sync().catch((e) => console.warn("brain-feedback: " + e.message));
  return `asked at ${new Date().toISOString()}; ${feedback.of.size} notes`;
}
// %%
feedbackGone = {
  annotations;
  if (!feedback) return "off";
  await feedback.gone();
  return feedback.of.size;
}
// %%
// A tracker and annotate's store, in memory, for the tests.
feedbackRig = () => {
  const issues = new Map(), calls = [], cells = new Map();
  let n = 0, at = 1000, clock = null;
  const client = {
    query: async (method, q = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, q]);
      if (method === "issue.list") return { issues: [...issues.values()].filter((t) => t.issue.labels.includes(q.label)).map((t) => ({ ...t.issue, body: undefined })) };
      if (method === "issue.get") return issues.has(q.id) ? structuredClone(issues.get(q.id)) : Promise.reject(new Error("no such issue"));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    },
    procedure: async (method, b = {}) => {
      calls.push([method, b]);
      if (method === "issue.open") {
        if (client.refuse) throw new Error(client.refuse);
        return void issues.set(b.id, { issue: { id: b.id, title: b.title, body: b.body, kind: b.kind, about: b.about, labels: [...b.labels], state: "open", closed: false, links: [], parent: null, updated_at: ++at }, events: [{ type: "opened", at, by: { caller: "owner" } }], children: [] });
      }
      if (method === "issue.label") return void ((t) => ((t.issue.labels = t.issue.labels.filter((l) => !b.remove.includes(l))), (t.issue.updated_at = ++at)))(issues.get(b.id));
      throw new Error("no " + method);
    }
  };
  // What the loop does to an issue between two reads.
  const say = (id, event, change = {}) => ((t) => (t.events.push({ at: ++at, by: { caller: "token", holder: "secret:issues-implementer-2" }, ...event }), Object.assign(t.issue, change, { updated_at: at })))(issues.get(id));
  const store = {
    all: () => [...cells.values()],
    get: (id) => cells.get(id) || null,
    create: (anchor, fields = {}) => ((a) => (cells.set(a.id, a), a))({ id: "a2t" + ++n, anchor, box: { dx: 120, dy: -80, w: 240 }, ...fields }),
    patch: (id, fields) => void (cells.has(id) && cells.set(id, { ...cells.get(id), ...fields })),
    remove: (id) => void cells.delete(id),
    refresh: async () => {}
  };
  // The page's clock: long after every event, until a test sets it.
  const now = () => (clock == null ? at + feedbackLimits.waitMs : clock);
  // The browser's copy of the notes not yet filed. A reload leaves it and takes every cell.
  let saved = null;
  const kept = { get: () => (saved == null ? null : JSON.parse(saved)), set: (all) => void (saved = JSON.stringify(all)) };
  return { client, store, issues, calls, cells, say, kept, reload: () => void cells.clear(), at: () => at, setNow: (ms) => void (clock = ms), app: (given = {}) => feedbackApp({ client, store, now, kept, ...given, near: () => "  Services\n table ", about: (a) => (a.module === "@tomlarkworthy/brain-issues" ? "brain-x-issues" : "brain") }) };
}
